## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design for policy drift in cross-tenant data sharing, integrating data contracts, policy-as-code, region controls, and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, policy_version, contract_id, tenant_id, region.
- Policy-as-code and a central contract registry.
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine.
- Minimal REST API for CAPAs linked to logs/traces.
- Metrics: recurrence_rate, MTTR, false_positive_rate by region/tenant; RCA template; canary rollout.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal REST endpoint sketch for creating a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  // validate body, persist CAPA, attach logs/traces
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate policy drift across regions automatically after a contract update?
- What telemetry would you add to detect cross-tenant leakage events in near real-time?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests building a CAPA program for cross-tenant log exposure caused by race conditions in multi-region deployments.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, redaction configs, tenantId, logs
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine
- Minimal REST API to link logs/traces
- Metrics: exposure rate, MTTR, false positives
- RCA template and canary rollout plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express API to create a CAPA
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const {tenantId, issue, evidence} = req.body;
  if(!tenantId || !issue) return res.status(400).send('bad input');
  // Persist CAPA skeleton (pseudo)
  res.status(201).send({id: 'capa-1', tenantId, issue});
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify false positives and tune the policy?
- What synthetic tests ensure coverage across regions during canary rollout?
